{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/config/validation_rules.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/config/validation_rules.py around lines 73 - 102, Extend FieldValidation.__post_init__ beyond discriminator checks to validate variant-specific parameters at construction: require range bounds to be present and ordered, compile pattern values and reject invalid regular expressions, require enum allowed values to be non-empty, and require custom validators to be provided. Raise the project’s established validation error with the relevant field/config context while preserving the existing freezing behavior and value-object invariants.","suggestions":["import re\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Convert lists to tuples for immutability.\"\"\"\n        require_literal(\n            self.validation_type,\n            field_name=\"validation_type\",\n            allowed=frozenset(\n                {\n                    \"required\",\n                    \"not_null\",\n                    \"range\",\n                    \"pattern\",\n                    \"enum\",\n                    \"max_length\",\n                    \"not_empty_list\",\n                    \"custom\",\n                }\n            ),\n        )\n        require_literal(\n            self.severity,\n            field_name=\"severity\",\n            allowed=frozenset({\"error\", \"warn\"}),\n        )\n        if self.severity_enricher is not None:\n            require_literal(\n                self.severity_enricher,\n                field_name=\"severity_enricher\",\n                allowed=frozenset({\"error\", \"warn\"}),\n            )\n        freeze_sequences(self, (\"allowed\",))\n        self._validate_variant()\n\n    def _validate_variant(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reject parameter sets that do not match ``validation_type``.\"\"\"\n        if self.validation_type == \"range\":\n            if self.min_value is None and self.max_value is None:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{self.field}: range validation requires min_value or max_value\"\n                )\n            if (\n                self.min_value is not None\n                and self.max_value is not None\n                and self.min_value > self.max_value\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{self.field}: min_value must not exceed max_value\"\n                )\n        elif self.validation_type == \"pattern\":\n            if self.pattern is None:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{self.field}: pattern validation requires pattern\")\n            try:\n                re.compile(self.pattern)\n            except re.error as exc:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{self.field}: pattern is not a valid regex: {self.pattern!r}\"\n                ) from exc\n        elif self.validation_type == \"enum\":\n            if not self.allowed:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{self.field}: enum validation requires a non-empty allowed set\"\n                )\n        elif self.validation_type == \"max_length\":\n            if self.max_length is None or self.max_length < 0:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{self.field}: max_length validation requires a non-negative max_length\"\n                )\n        elif self.validation_type == \"custom\" and not self.validator:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{self.field}: custom validation requires validator\")"]}
